            <section><h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#102338]">1. Who this notice covers</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">This notice describes information handled by Lumenix when you browse the public website, ask for a product walkthrough or pricing information, create an ISP workspace, or use the Lumenix platform. “Lumenix” is the platform brand. The operating entity and contact details are managed by the Lumenix platform team.</p></section>
            <section><h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#102338]">2. Information you provide</h2><ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600"><li>Public enquiries: name, ISP or company name, work email, optional phone number, topic of interest and message.</li><li>ISP workspace applications: ISP name, owner account details, country, currency/timezone defaults and brand settings.</li><li>Platform operations: staff account details, roles, billing records, router configuration and subscriber service/billing records entered by an ISP.</li></ul></section>
            <section><h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#102338]">3. How we use information</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">We use enquiry details to respond to the request and keep a record in the platform support queue. We use workspace and account information to provide authentication, tenant separation, billing, payment processing, router/RADIUS workflows, support, audit history and platform administration. We use operational data to display the states and reports requested by the ISP.</p></section>
            <section><h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#102338]">4. ISP data and payment providers</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">An ISP uses Lumenix to manage its subscribers and remains responsible for the subscriber relationship and its own customer billing. The platform keeps ISP customer collections separate from Lumenix SaaS billing. Payment and network integrations may exchange the information required to process a transaction or provide service with the provider configured by the ISP, such as M-Pesa/Daraja, FreeRADIUS or a MikroTik router. Provider systems have their own terms and privacy practices.</p></section>
            <section><h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#102338]">5. Storage, access and security</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">Workspace access is scoped by tenant membership and role. Passwords are stored using one-way password hashing; router credentials are encrypted in application storage; and selected administrative actions are recorded in audit logs. No online service can promise absolute security. ISPs should protect staff credentials, router access and provider accounts.</p></section>
            <section><h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#102338]">6. Retention and requests</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">Enquiries are retained in the platform support queue so the team can respond and keep a support history. ISP workspace, billing and audit records are retained to operate the service and preserve financial history. To ask about access, correction or deletion of information, submit a request through the <a class="font-semibold text-teal-800 underline" href="{{ route('home') }}#contact">Lumenix contact form</a>. Financial and security records may need to be retained where they support legitimate operational or legal obligations.</p></section>
